[05:55:10] │  summary="PR #2413 introduces normative rule 'mmode_req' mandating that all hardware implementations must provide M-mode as the highest privilege level with unfettered machine access. From the XiangShan RTL hardware security audit perspective, this single rule is the foundational requirement upon which all other privilege-based isolation mechanisms depend. If XiangShan were to violate this rule—by omitting M-mode, hardwiring priv_mode to a lower privilege, or failing to enforce M-mode exclusivity for privileged CSR access and instruction execution—the entire RISC-V security architecture collapses: PMP becomes meaningless, CSR access control dissolves, trap delegation is subvertible, and no trusted execution anchor exists. The affected hardware modules span the CSR unit, PMP checker, trap/interrupt controller, instruction decoder, TLB/PTW, reset controller, and multi-core interconnects. Verification of this rule requires confirming that priv_mode resets to M-mode, all M-mode CSR fields are only writable when priv_mode == M, M-mode-privileged instructions trap when executed from lower modes, and PMP configuration is exclusively an M-mode operation. This is priority-critical for XiangShan security assurance." entities=['[CSR Module] CSR.scala — priv-level access gating for all M-mode CSRs (mstatus, mtvec, mepc, mcause, mtval, mie, mip, medeleg, mideleg, mcycle, minstret, mhartid, marchid, mimpid, mvendorid, mscratch, mtinst, mtval2, pmpcfg*, pmpaddr*, mcounteren, menvcfg, mseccfg); reset state initialization of M-mode CSR fields. [PMP Checker] PMPChecker.scala — PMP rule enforcement depends on M-mode being the only configuration authority; PMP lock bits (L bit in pmpcfg) have no meaning without M-mode exclusivity. [Trap/Interrupt Controller] Control.scala / Trap.scala — trap delegation logic (medeleg/mideleg routing), exception priority encoding, MRET execution privilege check, privilege mode transition state machine. [Instruction Decoder] IDU.scala / Decoder.scala — privilege-check logic for MRET, WFI, SFENCE.VMA, and any future M-mode-privileged instructions; must reject these instructions when priv_mode != M. [TLB/PTW] TLB.scala / PTW.scala — page-table walker privilege mode context; SFENCE.VMA authority; virtual memory isolation depends on M-mode being able to invalidate TLB entries across all address spaces. [Reset Controller] Reset.scala / Boot.scala — reset vector configuration, initial priv_mode assignment at hart reset, CSR reset state sequencing. [Multi-Core Interconnect] — IMSIC/PLIC interrupt routing, cache coherence protocol privilege tagging, inter-hart interrupt (MSI) delivery, debug module cross-hart access control.']
[05:55:10] ╰─ Phase 1 done.
